.TH SBOM\-DIFF 1 "2026-09" "sbom-diff" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
sbom-diff \- diff two SBOMs and explain the changes in plain language
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sbom-diff
.I OLD
.I NEW
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Compares two SBOMs \(em CycloneDX JSON or SPDX JSON, as produced by syft,
trivy and others \(em and reports what was added, removed, upgraded,
downgraded or relicensed.
.PP
The gates are separate flags rather than one severity: a transitive
dependency appearing and a licence changing are different risks, and a
pipeline usually wants to fail on one and not the other.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-json
Machine-readable output.
.TP
.BI \-\-fail\-on " WHAT"
Exit 1 on
.BR any
change,
.B major
bumps, or
.B license
changes.
.TP
.BI \-\-max\-added " N"
Exit 1 if more than N components are added.
.TP
.BI \-\-max\-added\-transitive " N"
Exit 1 if more than N
.I transitive
components are added.
.TP
.B \-\-fail\-on\-downgrade
Exit 1 when a component moves to a lower version.
.TP
.B \-\-fail\-on\-license\-change
Exit 1 when an existing component changes licence.
.TP
.BI \-\-deny\-licenses " LIST"
Comma- or newline-separated licence identifiers that must not appear on an
added component.
.SS Review
The judgement layer: which of the changes a human should actually read.
.TP
.B \-\-review
Score every added and version-changed component against the signals and rank
the results into tiers, with the scoring rule printed in the report.
.TP
.B \-\-offline
Score only from the two SBOMs. Every signal that would need a network source
is reported as skipped, with the reason.
.TP
.BI \-\-disable\-signal " ID"
Turn one signal off. Repeatable, and accepts a comma-separated list.
.TP
.B \-\-list\-signals
Print every signal, its points and its source, then exit.
.TP
.BI \-\-fail\-on\-tier " TIER"
Exit 1 when any component lands in
.BR read ,
.BR glance
or
.BR routine
\(em or any louder tier.
.TP
.BI \-\-young\-days " N"
Flag releases published less than N days ago (default 14).
.TP
.BI \-\-fanout\-threshold " N"
Flag a component whose transitive count grew by more than N (default 5).
.TP
.BI \-\-scorecard\-drop " POINTS"
Flag an OpenSSF Scorecard fall larger than this (default 1.0).
.TP
.BI \-\-cache\-dir " PATH"
Where responses are cached. Defaults to
.IR $XDG_CACHE_HOME/sbom-diff .
.TP
.BI \-\-cache\-ttl " SECONDS"
How long a cached response stays fresh (default 86400).
.TP
.B \-\-no\-cache
Do not read or write the response cache.
.TP
.BI \-\-max\-requests " N"
Stop asking after N requests in one run (default 300, 0 for no limit).
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
No gate was breached.
.TP
.B 1
A gate was breached.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Diff two syft SBOMs:
.PP
.RS
.B sbom-diff old.json new.json
.RE
.PP
Gate a release on licences and transitive growth:
.PP
.RS
.B sbom-diff old.json new.json \-\-fail\-on\-license\-change \-\-max\-added\-transitive 5
.RE
.PP
Rank what to read, and fail the build on anything in the loudest tier:
.PP
.RS
.B sbom-diff old.json new.json \-\-review \-\-fail\-on\-tier read
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR syft (1),
.BR trivy (1),
.BR scan-image (1).
